## 2. Describe Your Recent Experience With Similar Projects

I recently completed a centralized logging and observability project on Rocky Linux 9, a Red Hat-compatible platform.

I built a Docker-based monitoring server using Grafana, Loki, Grafana Alloy, Prometheus, and Node Exporter. A second Rocky Linux VM was configured to forward operating-system logs reliably over TCP to the monitoring server.

The work included configuring remote syslog forwarding, validating RFC 5424 log formatting, opening the required firewalld ports, assigning a non-standard TCP port to the correct SELinux `syslogd_port_t` context, and troubleshooting an SELinux “Permission denied” forwarding issue.

I verified the complete flow using `rsyslogd -N1`, `systemctl`, `journalctl`, `nc`, `tcpdump`, and the `logger` command. Logs were successfully received by Grafana Alloy, stored in Loki, and displayed in Grafana with labels for hostname, application, severity, facility, transport, and source IP.

I also created LogQL searches and graphical counts to show incoming logs by host and over time. This project closely matches the logging, retention, source tracking, troubleshooting, and graphical monitoring requirements in your job description.

